<title>USA: Reeths-Puffer Schs, Mich., won by First of America. [CORRECTED 20:14 GMT]</title>
<headline>Reeths-Puffer Schs, Mich., won by First of America. [CORRECTED 20:14 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>First of America Securities said it won $4.900 million of Reeths-Puffer Schools, Mich., general obligation 1996 school building and site bonds, with a net interest cost of 5.485 percent.  </p>
<p>AMT: 4,900,000	DATE: 11/04/96	NYC Time: 1100	CUSIP: 758508     </p>
<p>ISSUER: Reeths-Puffer Schools					 ST: MI		</p>
<p>ISSUE: G.O. 1996 school building &amp; site			   TAX STAT:Exempt-ULT</p>
<p>M/SP/F: NA/NA/NA							  BOOK ENTRY: Y     </p>
<p>ENHANCEMENTS: FGIC AAA/AAA/NR					 BANK QUAL: Y	</p>
<p>DTD: 11/01/96							     SURE BID: Y	 </p>
<p>DUE: 5/1/97-26						SR MGR: First of America    </p>
<p>1ST CPN: 05/01/97					   DOLLAR BID: 98.75	     </p>
<p>CALL: 5/1/06 @ par					  NIC 5.485			 </p>
<p>DELIVERY: 45 days					   ORDERS: 1 HR		    </p>
<p>PAYING AGENT: Old Kent Bank, Grand Rapids						 </p>
<p>L.O.: Thrun, Maatsch and Nordberg, Lansing						</p>
<p>F.A.: Stauder, Barch &amp; Associates, Inc., Ann Arbor				    </p>
